<html>
<head>
<title>Saw Banners Be Gone!</title> 
<link href="/sCSS/8.0/Theme2/default/common.css" rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" />
<script src="/dJS/en/library.js"></script>
<script type="text/javascript">
{!INCLUDE($SControl.SawBannersBGone__hpcApi)}

{!INCLUDE($SControl.SawBannersBGone__GenericHpcInstaller)}

{!INCLUDE($SControl.SawBannersBGone__sbgInstaller)}

var sbg = new sbgInstaller();
</script>
<style>
body {
	margin-left: 3em;
}
</style>

<script type="text/javascript">
function showManualInstall() {
	document.getElementById('manualInstallation').style.display='block';
	document.getElementById('automatedInstallation').style.display='none';
	return false;
}
</script>
</head>
<body>
<div><img src="/servlet/servlet.ImageServer?id=01550000000K4JU&oid=00D300000000W1h" width='749' height='322'></div>
<h3>You asked for it and we delivered.</h3>

<p><em>Saw Banners Be Gone!</em> works by embedding some javascript in all of the custom home-pages in your org.<BR/>
If you have problems with the automated script, try the <a href="#" onclick="showManualInstall();">manual installation instructions</a>.</p>

<div id='automatedInstallation'>
<h3>Easy 1-click install</h3>
<ul><li>Click <input class='btn' type='button' value='here' onclick="sbg.install();this.disabled = true; this.className='btnDisabled'; this.value = 'Please Wait...'; "> to install <em>SawBannersBeGone!</em> </li></ul>
</div>

<div id='manualInstallation' style='display:none'>
<h3>Manual Installation instructions</h3>
<p>You need to follow these instructions only if the automated script proves unsuccessful.</p>
<ol>
<li> Paste the following snippet into your <strong>Messages &amp; Alerts</strong> note by clicking edit on <a href = '/setup/ui/homepagecomponents.jsp?retURL=%2Fui%2Fsetup%2FSetup%3Fsetupid%3DHome&setupid=HomePageComponents'>this page</a><BR> <textarea rows='3' cols='70' id='installationContent'>
{!INCLUDE($SControl.SawBannersBGone__sbgContent)}
</textarea></li>
<li>Ensure that the <strong>Messages &amp; Alerts</strong> note appears on all users' home pages. </li>
<li> Celebrate!</li>
</ol>
</div>

</body>
</html>